\title{2026-W41}
\date{2026-10-05}

\p{Start contributing to Tau Ceti's \strong{DifferentialGeometry} roadmap: forms, the exterior derivative and their calculus, orientations, flows, distributions, de Rham cohomology and duality, mapping degree, planar Green, and the Riemannian calculus along the route of Lee's \em{Introduction to Smooth Manifolds}, begun from an interest in geometric calculus; parts of it may be recovered in the discrete-induced work where needed, though they are not its focus, see [the route map](https://utensil.github.io/formal-land/dg/dg-route-map.html).}

